A bundled complete lattice is a type together with a complete-lattice structure, so the function-space tower can be defined by recursion. `towerCLat` begins with the given lattice D_0, and the successor of level n is the complete lattice of Scott maps from the carrier of level n to itself. `towerType` is that carrier. `towerCompleteLattice` gives each level the complete-lattice structure of its bundle. `towerType_succ` says level n+1 is definitionally the Scott maps from level n to itself, and `towerType_zero` says level 0 is definitionally the carrier of the starting lattice. `towerToMap` views an element of level n+1 as that Scott map, `towerCoeFun` applies it as a function of the preceding level, and `towerToMap_coe` says that application agrees with applying the element itself. The successor, zero, and coercion facts are definitional.
